---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
List the instrumented code locations of a run, and when the run first reached
each one.

Each row is one location: MODULE, LOCATION, FUNCTION, HASH and VTIME. MODULE is
the module ID that `runs modules` lists. LOCATION is the source file, line and
column. HASH and VTIME give the moment where the run first reached the location,
and are blank for a location that the run has not reached. Pass them as the
input_hash and vtime of `runs logs` to read the logs up to that moment. The rows
give no container: to show the coverage of one container, pass the module IDs
that `runs modules` lists for it.

Use --module to show only the locations of a module. Give it more than once for
more modules. Use --reached to show only the locations that the run reached, and
--unreached to show only the locations that it did not reach. While the run is
in progress, the output is the coverage up to now.

VTIME is cut to five decimals. With --detail, it prints whole. On a terminal, a
long LOCATION or FUNCTION is shortened. After the rows, a status line on stderr
counts the locations, and gives the run's status.

With --follow, the command prints the locations that the run reached, then each
new location as the run reaches it, until the run finishes. Without --reached, a
location prints again when the run reaches it. --follow cannot be used with
--unreached.

With --json, each location prints as the JSON object that the API sends, on its
own line. A reached location has `first_reached`, with the moment and
`run_seconds`, the time in seconds from the start of the run. So
`snouty runs coverage <run_id> --json > coverage.ndjson` downloads the coverage.
If the server reports an error during the output, snouty prints its error line,
and exits with status 3.

Examples:
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --reached --module <module_id>
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --unreached --module <module_id>
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --reached --follow

Usage: snouty runs coverage [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --module <MODULE_ID>
          Only list the locations of this module (repeatable)

      --reached
          Only list the locations that the run reached

      --unreached
          Only list the locations that the run has not reached

  -f, --follow
          Keep the connection open, and print each location as the run reaches
          it, until the run finishes

  -d, --detail
          Print each vtime whole

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print NDJSON: one JSON object per line

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
